    <statement><p>Evaluate the double integral of the function over the rectangle :</p>
<p><me>\int\!\!\int _{\mathcal{R}} \frac{y}{x+1}\,dA ,\quad\mathcal{R}=[0,24]\times[0,16]</me>
Answer : <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>412.016</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f( x,y )=g(x)h(y)</m>.



<me>\begin{array}{rcl}
\int\!\!\int _{\mathcal{R}}\frac{y}{x+1} \,dA\amp =\amp 
\int_0^{16}\int_0^{24}\frac{y}{x+1} \,dx\,dy\\
\amp =\amp 
\left(\int_0^{24}\frac{dx}{x+1}\right)\left(\int_0^{16}y \,dy\right)\\
\amp =\amp \left(\ln(x+1)\bigg|_0^{24}\right)\left(\frac{{y}^2}{2}\bigg|_0^{16}\right)\\
\amp =\amp 
(\ln 25- \ln 1 )\left(\frac{{16}^2}{2}-\frac{{0}^2}{2}\right)\\
\amp =\amp 
128 \ln 25 \approx 412.016
\end{array}</me>



</solution>
